# Spinifex RDS generated-configuration include.
#
# The generated files live on the data volume rather than under /etc. A class
# change is a VM replacement: a fresh boot volume with the same data volume
# reattached. Parameters under /etc would be discarded by that replacement and
# the instance would silently revert to catalog defaults while the API still
# reported the customer's values.
#
# This directory, not Alpine's /etc/my.cnf.d: Debian and Ubuntu route
# /etc/mysql/my.cnf to mariadb.cnf, which reads conf.d/ first and
# mariadb.conf.d/ second. zz- so this also sorts last within it — MariaDB walks
# an include directory in byte order and takes the last occurrence of a
# setting, and a digit prefix would sort ahead of the packaged 50-server.cnf.
# The postinst asserts both halves against the real image at build time.
#
# The target directory is baked empty into the image: MariaDB treats an
# !includedir it cannot open as a fatal defaults-parsing error, so a boot with
# no data volume would otherwise take the client down with the server.

!includedir /var/lib/mysql/conf.d
